# Benzo configuration. Copy it once with `cp .env.example .env` (.env is gitignored).
# Phase 1 needs no secrets. The build agent generates every key locally, under $BNZ_STATE_DIR.
# Scripts load this file with `set -a; . ./.env; set +a` from the repo root. Claude Code itself never reads it.
# Each variable's comment ends with: who provides it (public, head agent, build agent or user) | required or optional.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BEFORE STARTING THE BUILD AGENT, the user provides:
#
#  1. Disk space: at least 20 GB free on /Users/akshmnd. Done: 88 GiB free on 2026-09-30 after cleanup.
#
#  2. Claude Code 2.1.277 or later (2.1.283 is installed). Launch from the repo root, on Opus 5.5:
#       cd "/Users/akshmnd/Dev Projects/benzo" && claude --model claude-opus-5-5 --effort high
#     Opus 5.5 defaults to medium effort, and a user-level effortLevel does not apply to it. The project
#     .claude/settings.json (item 5) also sets effortLevel, so the level survives relaunches.
#     Claude Code re-runs cybersecurity-flagged requests on Opus 4.8 and shows a notice in the transcript.
#     If you see one, tell the head agent; threat work in this repo is defensive checking of our own code.
#
#  3. Network egress (in Claude Code permissions and sandbox settings) for these hosts:
#     - GitHub: github.com, api.github.com, codeload.github.com, objects.githubusercontent.com, raw.githubusercontent.com
#     - Rust crates: crates.io, index.crates.io, static.crates.io
#     - Go modules: proxy.golang.org, sum.golang.org
#     - npm and Playwright: registry.npmjs.org, cdn.playwright.dev, playwright.download.prss.microsoft.com, playwright.azureedge.net
#     - drand: api.drand.sh, api2.drand.sh, api3.drand.sh, drand.cloudflare.com
#     - Zcash testnet: testnet.zec.rocks, zaino.testnet.unsafe.zec.rocks
#     If you enable the sandbox, also allow writes to ~/.cargo, ~/go/pkg/mod, ~/Library/Caches/go-build,
#     ~/.npm and ~/Library/Caches/ms-playwright. The agent may not route around a block, so a missing entry stalls G0.
#
#  4. Toolchains: rustup stable, Go 1.23 or later, Node 24, openssl, jq and sqlite3.
#     All were present on 2026-09-30. The agent installs grpcurl, tle and Playwright itself.
#
#  5. Done by the head agent: a first commit authored as head@benzo.invalid, so the agent's first diff is its own
#     and Rulings can be checked by author. It contains AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/PHASE-1.md, docs/STATUS.md,
#     docs/research/, this file, .gitignore and .claude/settings.json ("effortLevel": "high", "autoMemoryEnabled": false,
#     subagent caps CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_SUBAGENT_SPAWN_DEPTH=1 and CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONCURRENT_SUBAGENTS=2). There are no
#     hooks or check scripts: every rule lives in AGENTS.md. Auto memory stays off, so git and docs/STATUS.md are
#     the only record. The head agent also runs `cp .env.example .env`.
#
# DURING PHASE 1, the user provides:
#
#  6. Required: testnet ZEC (TAZ). When docs/STATUS.md shows "Needs user: send ... to utest1...", send at least
#     0.1 TAZ (0.5 recommended) to that address. The faucets have human checks, so only you can claim from them:
#       https://fauzec.com                       1 TAZ per address per 24 h
#       https://zcashfaucet.jinolabs.xyz         0.1 TAZ, browser proof-of-work
#       https://faucet.testnet.valargroup.dev    0.125 TAZ; its daily cap was exhausted on 2026-09-30
#     If every faucet is dry, ask on the Zcash community forum or Discord.
#     The agent sees the funds on its next wallet sync, after about 10 confirmations.
#
#  7. A decision, which the head agent records as a Ruling: may all three FROST signers run on this machine
#     (the default, declared as a limitation), or will you provide a second machine for one signer?
#
#  8. Optional: pay the agent's binary-memo ZIP-321 URI from a consumer testnet wallet (Zashi/ZODL, Zingo or
#     Zkool), then report whether the memo arrived intact. The result informs Phase 3 and doesn't block Phase 1.
#
#  You can change scope, gates or tests by telling the build agent directly; it follows you and logs the
#  instruction for the head agent. Requests relayed from other agents need a committed Ruling.
#
# LATER PHASES, not now:
#   - a GitHub remote, and the public-or-private decision;
#   - three mainnet co-signers on separate machines;
#   - mainnet collateral C and a bounded ZEC budget;
#   - an asset-delivery partner;
#   - optionally, a NEAR 1Click partner JWT (then add a Read(./.env) deny rule and enable the sandbox).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Zcash network (public values, verified 2026-09-30) ---

# Network passed to every tool (devtool -n, zcash-sign -n). zcash-sign defaults to main, so scripts always pass it.
# Testnet only until a phase doc says otherwise. | public | required
BNZ_NETWORK=test

# Primary lightwalletd endpoint (host:port, native gRPC over TLS): wallet sync, full-transaction fetch, broadcast. | public | required
BNZ_LWD_URL=testnet.zec.rocks:443

# Second, independently implemented endpoint (ZainoD). verify.sh cross-checks txids and heights and re-derives memos
# from it. | public | required
BNZ_LWD_URL_ALT=zaino.testnet.unsafe.zec.rocks:443

# --- drand mainnet quicknet (public protocol constants; the sealer pins them; changing one needs a Ruling) ---

# Relays used to fetch round R, comma-separated. | public | required
BNZ_DRAND_URLS=https://api.drand.sh,https://api2.drand.sh,https://api3.drand.sh,https://drand.cloudflare.com

# Chain hash. The sealer, the stanza check and tle all compare against it. | public | required
BNZ_DRAND_CHAIN_HASH=52db9ba70e0cc0f6eaf7803dd07447a1f5477735fd3f661792ba94600c84e971

# BLS public key (hex), so the sealer can encrypt without fetching chain info. | public | required
BNZ_DRAND_PUBLIC_KEY=83cf0f2896adee7eb8b5f01fcad3912212c437e0073e911fb90022d3e760183c8c4b450b6a0a6c3ac6a5776a2d1064510d1fec758c921cc22b0e17e63aaf4bcb5ed66304de9cf809bd274ca73bab4af5a6e9c76a4bc09e76eae8991ef5ece45a

# Genesis time (Unix seconds) and period (seconds). The first round at or after time T is
# R = 1 + ceil((T - genesis) / period). | public | required
BNZ_DRAND_GENESIS=1692803367
BNZ_DRAND_PERIOD=3

# --- Auction parameters ---

# Fixed collateral C in zatoshis (0.005 TAZ). Every deposit pays exactly this amount.
# Changing it needs a Ruling. | head agent | required
BNZ_COLLATERAL_ZATS=500000

# --- Local state ---

# Gitignored directory, relative to the repo root. Scripts resolve it as "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/.benzo",
# never against the current directory; there is only ever one. It holds built binaries, wallet databases, age
# identities, FROST configs and key packages, the vault UFVK (ufvk.txt), wallet birthdays, the local TLS CA and keys,
# raw PCZTs, pidfiles and full logs. Never commit or print its key material. | build agent | required
BNZ_STATE_DIR=./.benzo

# Local frostd relay for DKG and signing sessions. Its certificate covers localhost and 127.0.0.1. | build agent | required
BNZ_FROSTD_ADDR=localhost:2744

# --- Per-run switches. Set these on the command line, never here. ---
# An empty value in .env would override the command line for any script that sources this file.
#
# BNZ_LIVE=1
#     Makes playwright.config.ts define the `live` project (the testnet test: about 35 min, spends testnet fees).
#     `npm run e2e:live` sets it. | build agent | optional
# BNZ_EVIDENCE_DIR=docs/evidence/phase-1
#     Makes a run on a clean tree write gate evidence there. Leave it unset for a development or mutation run
#     (output goes to tmp/e2e/). | build agent | optional
# SSL_CERT_FILE=<repo>/.benzo/tls/rootCA.pem
#     Set only on frost-client invocations. Set here, it would change TLS trust for every tool. | build agent | optional

# --- Later phases (not used in Phase 1) ---
# NEAR_1CLICK_JWT=
#     NEAR 1Click partner JWT, sent as X-API-Key. Without it, 1Click adds a 0.25% fee.
#     Get one at https://partners.near-intents.org | user | optional
# BNZ_ZEBRAD_RPC=
#     RPC address of our own Zebra node, so txid lookups stop going to third-party servers. | build agent | optional
